0338-negroni-bt-le-legacy-to-extended: legacy LE scan/advertising/connect commands become extended ones on the QCA6490.

Phone [V] 2026-10-27 04:06 (logs/usblog-20261026-233816.txt, kernel local-20261026-222425 with 0335-0337): every Apple
VSC passes (0337 works), then "h4 tx cmd 0x200b plen 7: 01 0b 20 07 00 e0 01 30 00 01 00" -> "Command Complete op
0x200b status 0xc" (Command Disallowed) -> "exit bluetoothd status 1", every ~10 s (launchd restart; 0335 powers the
chip off/on each time). 0x2007 (also legacy) gets 0x0c at init as well. The host sent no extended LE command before:
the controller firmware (BTFW.HSP.2.1.0-00394) takes only the extended LE command set [I strong]. bluetoothd uses the
legacy set on this chip (its chipset table says extended scan/advertising disabled).
This crash loop is also why Bluetooth cannot be turned off in Settings [I]: bluetoothd dies ~1 s after each start, so
the switch request has no running daemon to act on. The power-off path itself [V disassembly of 20H392 bluetoothd]:
"Beginning asynchronous power shutdown" -> StackManager halts the core stack -> applebt_transport_terminate ->
applebt_hci_close (the control socket closes: 0335 drives BT_EN low 3 s later) -> "Powering off chipset" (BlueTool
"deepsleep" script, negroni-bluetool answers 0).

negroni_bt_shim.c (negronibt_lext=1 default, 0 = old pass-through):
- 0x200b -> 0x2041, 0x200c -> 0x2042 (answers: op rewritten in place), 0x200d -> 0x2043 (Command Status op rewritten).
- 0x2006/0x2008/0x2009/0x200a -> advertising set 0: 0x2036/0x2037/0x2038/0x2039, run as a chain (one command at a
  time; the RX thread sends the next after the answer; then one legacy Command Complete). 0x2036 gets 0x2035 (set
  random address) after it when the own address type is random; 0x2005 gets 0x2035 after it when set 0 exists. A
  data/enable command before any 0x2006 creates set 0 with the legacy defaults first.
- LE Extended Advertising Report -> one LE Advertising Report per legacy-PDU report (extended PDUs, anonymous and
  > 31-byte reports dropped). LE Advertising Set Terminated / Scan Timeout dropped. 0x2001 gets bit 12.
- 0337 review: table names fixed (0xfce2 sub 0x1c = SET_MIN_AFH_LE_CHANNELS; 0xfd48 = an address command [I]).
negroni_bt_h4.c: negroni_bt_h4_send_cmd (TX path with IBS wake; from the RX thread without h4_tx; when the
controller said SLEEP_IND, the power worker sends it after ibs_wake with h4_tx held).
Opus review 2026-10-27 (ACCEPT with fixes), fixed here: F1 legacy report plen 12 + data (was 11: stream desync and a
1-byte stack overflow at 31 data bytes); F2 set 0 exists only after 0x2036 status 0; F3 high-duty directed enable
gets duration 0x0080 (1.28 s); F4 0x2008 on a directed set and non-empty 0x2009 on a non-scannable set get a local
status 0 (legacy ignores that data, 0x2037/0x2038 would answer 0x12); F5 no RX-thread send to a sleeping controller;
F6 a chain without an answer for 2 s is dropped at the next advertising command; F8 locking comment; F10 log fixes.
Host test: scripts/kernel/test-bt-shim.sh TREE (tools/bt-shim-test, ASan + UBSan).

